## Quality checks

Run these before marking a task complete. Do not skip them.

```bash
make format       # auto-format
make lint         # linting + type checking
make test         # full test suite
make check-arch   # architecture boundary check
```

If `make check-arch` reports violations, read the REMEDIATION instruction
in each violation and fix the import before continuing.

## Completing a task

- All quality checks pass
- If a plan was created: check off completed steps, update the decision log
- Do **not** open a pull request — the human reviewer will do this
- If the task addressed known debt: update `docs/quality.md`

## Proof of work

When complete, provide:
- Summary of what was implemented
- Which files were changed and why
- Results of `make test` and `make check-arch`
- Any decisions made that weren't in the original plan
